<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Synthetic C-CDA Results section. No patient data.

  The structured entries reproduce the referenceRange shapes one vendor's
  export uses, which a reader that takes observationRange's whole text content
  stores doubled ("NEGNEG", "mIU/mLmIU/mL", "4.3 - 5.6 PERCENTPERCENTPERCENT"):

    lab-st-neg          <text>NEG</text> plus <value xsi:type="ST">NEG</value>
    lab-st-detected     the same shape with a two-word string
    lab-unit-only       the same shape where the string is only the unit, on a
                        REAL result that names no unit of its own
    lab-ivl-ucum        a normal IVL_PQ with <text> and UCUM low/high
    lab-ivl-translation IVL_PQ whose bounds are nullFlavor PQs carrying the
                        number in translation/@value and a non-UCUM unit in
                        translation/originalText, once per bound
    lab-ivl-no-text     IVL_PQ with no <text>: an exclusive upper bound only
    lab-text-reference  <text> that points into the narrative by reference
    lab-interval-value  a result that is itself an interval ("<30")
    lab-ed-reference    an ED value, the range text and the interpretation that
                        each hold only a reference into the narrative

  The narrative table mirrors that vendor's column order (Component, Value,
  Ref Range, Test Method, Analysis Time), which is not the order the
  narrative-table reader assumes. As in that export, each observation's <text>
  references the Component cell of its own row, which is how a row imported
  through the narrative table is matched to its observation.
-->
